s><patcit ucid="EP-0173380-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>EP</country><doc-number>0173380</doc-number><kind>A1</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9012804-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9012804</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1029876A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>ASAHI CHEMICAL IND</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>SASAYA EIJI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>YONEZAWA JUN</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>ASAHI KASEI KOGYO KABUSHIKI KAISHA</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>SASAYA, EIJI</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>YONEZAWA, JUN</last-name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>SASAYA EIJI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>YONEZAWA JUN</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>SASAYA, EIJI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>YONEZAWA, JUN</last-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A hydrogenated block copolymer which is made up of at least two polymer blocks A consisting mainly of vinylaromatic hydrocarbon compound units and at least two polymer blocks B consisting mainly of hydrogenated butadiene units and in which the polymer blocks B each has a degree of hydrogenation of 90 % or higher, wherein at least one of the terminal blocks is a polymer block B, all the terminal polymer blocks B account for 0.1 to 9.1 wt%, excluding 9.1 wt.%, of the whole copolymer, the vinylaromatic hydrocarbon compound units account for 25 to 80 wt.%, excluding 80 wt%, of the whole copolymer, and the polymer blocks B before hydrogenation had a 1,2-bond content of 60 to 99 mol%, excluding 99 mol%, on the average.  A resin composition is also provided which comprises the copolymer and either a polypropylene resin/a polyphenylene ether resin or a polystyrene resin.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Copolymère bloc hydrogéné qui est composé d'au moins deux blocs polymères A constitués principalement d'unités de composé hydrocarbure vinylaromatiques et d'au moins deux blocs polymères B constitués principalement d'unités butadiène hydrogénées, et dans lequel les blocs polymères B présentent chacun un degré d'hydrogénation de 90 % ou plus. Ledit copolymère est caractérisé en ce qu'au moins un des blocs terminaux est un bloc polymère B, l'ensemble des blocs polymères terminaux B représente de 0,1 à moins de 9,1 % en poids du copolymère total, les unités de composé hydrocarbure vinylaromatiques représentent de 25 à moins de 80 % en poids du copolymère total et les blocs polymères B avant hydrogénation possèdent une teneur en liaison 1,2 de 60 à moins de 99 moles pour cent en moyenne. La présente invention concerne également une composition de résine qui comporte ledit copolymère et soit une résine polypropylène/polyéther de phénylène, soit une résine polystyrène.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>